    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n130 Gaybrook Lawns is an exceptional semi-detached family home situated in the quiet, mature and sought-after development convenient to Malahide Village and within walking distance of the pedestrian gate to Malahide CastleBeautifully maintained and presented by the current owners, the property offers a refined blend of space, light, and design, resulting in a home of genuine quality and style.The accommodation has been carefully designed to suit modern family living. At ground floor level there is an elegant reception and dining room providing excellent space for both everyday living and entertaining. To the rear, a bright open-plan kitchen and sunroom overlook the manicured rear garden, creating a wonderful heart to the home. Cleverly designed fitted units and large kitchen island, provide excellent additional storage while maintaining a sleek and practical kitchen layout. The garage has been converted to provide a large utility room which acts as a seamless extension of the kitchen with dedicated extra storage, worktops and additional appliances. Upstairs, there are four spacious bedrooms and a contemporary family bathroom, all finished to a very high standard.Outside the front garden has been extensively paved to provide off street parking for two cars. The front part of the garage conversion has been divided to incorporate storage for bikes and bins. The beautifully landscaped rear garden enjoys a wonderfully tranquil setting. Set around a manicured grass lawn bound by raised bed with colourful shrubbery it has been thoughtfully designed as a natural extension of the house itself, creating a series of inviting outdoor spaces for relaxation, entertaining and family life.Viewing is essential to really appreciate this excellent family residence in this desirable and convenient location."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 3.26m x 3.00m\nLarge entrance hall with double glazed windows allowing for an abundance of natural light, ornate coving on ceiling, large porcelain tile flooring, upgraded solid wood front door.\n\nGuest Wc - 1.80m x 0.83m\nTiled guest wc with hand wash basin and wc\n\nLiving/ Dining room - 10.00m x 3.63m\nLarge reception room with living room to front, large double glazed window with electric blinds, Henley wood burning fire. Dining room to rear with access to kitchen and French doors opening onto landscaped rear garden. Coving on ceiling, feature wall panelling and solid wooden flooring throughout.\n\nKitchen/ Breakfast Room - 5.53m x 5.10m\nBright open-plan kitchen with cleverly designed fitted units, high quality integrated appliances and large kitchen island, quartz work tops throughout and extensive utility room off provides excellent additional storage. Large porcelain tile flooring throughout and French doors to rear, Sunroom off kitchen.\n\nUtility Room - 3.61m x 2.33m\nThe garage has been converted to provide a large utility room which acts as a seamless extension of the kitchen with dedicated extra storage, pvc ceiling, worktops and additional appliances.\n\nSunroom - 4.00m x 3.30m\nTiled sunroom with double glazed windows and French doors off kitchen. Electric blinds.\n\nLanding - 3.03m x 2.26m\nLarge landing with double glazed windows and carpet flooring\n\nPrincipal Bedroom - 4.12m x 3.65m\nLarge bedroom with built in wardrobes, two double glazed windows to front with plantation shutters, carpet flooring\n\nEnsuite - 2.14m x 0.85m\nShower, hand wash basin with storage, fully tiled\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.62m x 3.63m\nLarge bedroom with built in slide robes, two double glazed windows to rear with plantation shutters, laminate wood flooring\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.95m x 2.35m\nDouble glazed window to rear with plantation shutters, built in wardrobe\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.04m x 2.22\nDouble glazed window to rear with plantation shutters, Laminate wood flooring\n\nBathroom - 2.33m x 1.93m\nFully tiled family bathroom, bath with shower, large wash hand basin with storage, wc\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Sought-after Development convenient to Malahide Village and Malahide Castle</li><li>Semi detached</li><li>Wonderfully maintained and presented throughout</li><li>Sunroom extension</li><li>Large utility Room</li><li>Four bedrooms</li><li>Large landscaped rear garden </li><li>Gas fired central heating</li><li>Ample parking space for multiple cars</ul>"
      },
